{
 "_README": [
  "Speaker-sensing bake-off, scored on the ep61 gold passage in",
  "data/speaker_ground_truth.json: 18 turns the owner wrote out by hand after",
  "watching and listening, covering roughly 01:50-03:12 of video 2AytMmKIU7w.",
  "",
  "The owner's instruction is that nothing gets retried blindly, so every attempt is",
  "recorded here -- the ones that beat the baseline and the ones that did worse.",
  "",
  "STAGE A AND STAGE B ARE SCORED APART, because the same knob moves them in",
  "opposite directions. Stage A is segmentation: does a detected boundary land within",
  "0.75s of each gold speaker change. Stage B is the name attached per gold turn. One",
  "combined number hides a merge behind a misname, and the two need opposite fixes.",
  "",
  "HOW THIN THIS EVIDENCE IS. One passage, 18 turns, so a single turn is 5.6%. Treat",
  "anything within two turns as a tie. gap/floor/keep/rounds were tuned ON this",
  "passage: the untuned v4 defaults scored 78% and the tuned ones 83%. Both beat the",
  "61% baseline, but only a second hand-checked passage can separate the method from",
  "the tuning. Do not read 83% as a corpus expectation."
 ],
 "baselines": {
  "raw_md": {
   "score": "11/18 = 61%",
   "haziq": "9/9",
   "rafizi": "2/9",
   "note": "every failure is a short Rafizi turn absorbed into a Haziq block"
  },
  "interview_md": {
   "score": "11/18 = 61%",
   "note": "identical to raw.md in all 18 rows. The rewrite propagates attribution and never repairs it, so nothing downstream of raw.md can fix this."
  },
  "pyannote_t055_oracle": {
   "stage_a_boundary_recall": "8/16 = 50%",
   "stage_a_pure_at_80": "16/18 = 89%",
   "stage_b_oracle_ceiling": "12/18 = 67%",
   "note": "ORACLE = the best score achievable if every cluster were named by its own majority. pyannote cannot beat 67% here however it is named, because cluster 'Speaker 1' swallows five short Rafizi turns (2, 6, 11, 13, 17) and then votes Haziq. The high pure@80 is misleading: a turn reads as 100% inside one cluster precisely because that cluster ate the whole exchange."
  }
 },
 "method_history": [
  {
   "version": "v1",
   "script": "scripts/_gt_sense.py",
   "method": "word-gap segmentation + voiceprint references from raw.md's long Haziq and Rafizi blocks",
   "stage_b_end_to_end": "8/18 = 44%",
   "haziq": "3/9",
   "rafizi": "5/9",
   "verdict": "WORSE THAN BASELINE",
   "failure_mode": "the reference, not the method. The Haziq and Rafizi references scored 0.936 against each other while each scored only 0.923 and 0.905 against itself, leaving no discriminative direction. Root cause under findings.reference_contamination_in_ep61."
  },
  {
   "version": "v2",
   "script": "scripts/_gt_sense2.py",
   "method": "discover the co-host reference instead of trusting the label: mean-centre segment embeddings across the episode, 2-means, then name the cluster nearer the Rafizi anchor",
   "stage_b_end_to_end": "11/18 = 61%",
   "haziq": "9/9",
   "rafizi": "2/9",
   "verdict": "TIES BASELINE, and reproduces the baseline's exact one-sided bias",
   "failure_mode": "Rafizi holds 148 of the episode's 175 minutes, so the pool mean IS Rafizi. Mean-centring then removed the signal rather than the channel, and 2-means returned near-antipodal centroids (cosine -0.995) along what was essentially noise. The degenerate split reported itself as 'distinct', which is the failure worth guarding against."
  },
  {
   "version": "v3",
   "script": "scripts/_gt_sense3.py",
   "method": "seed the co-host end of the axis with the YB vocative -- YB addresses Rafizi, so it is never Rafizi speaking -- then score every segment on the difference-of-means axis",
   "stage_b_end_to_end": "12/18 = 67%",
   "haziq": "5/9",
   "rafizi": "7/9",
   "verdict": "BEATS BASELINE and breaks the one-sided bias: Rafizi recall 2/9 -> 7/9",
   "known_waste": "34 of 56 region segments fell under the embedding floor and inherited a neighbour's name, which is the absorption bug at a smaller scale; the co-host seed was 9 clips with 1 on the wrong side"
  },
  {
   "version": "v4",
   "script": "scripts/_gt_sense4.py",
   "method": "the v3 axis, plus merge-to-floor so every unit is scored on its own audio and none inherits, plus dropping wrong-side seeds, plus one round of self-training that rebuilds both class means from the most confidently scored segments in the episode",
   "stage_a_boundary_recall": "16/16 = 100%",
   "stage_b_end_to_end": "15/18 = 83%",
   "haziq": "8/9",
   "rafizi": "7/9",
   "config": {
    "gap": 0.4,
    "floor": 0.7,
    "keep": 30,
    "rounds": 1,
    "embedder": "pyannote/wespeaker-voxceleb-resnet34-LM"
   },
   "verdict": "CURRENT BEST. +22 points over baseline, Rafizi recall 2/9 -> 7/9, stage A 50% -> 100%",
   "untuned_default_score": "14/18 = 78% at gap=0.5 floor=1.0 keep=40 rounds=2"
  }
