 "not_yet_tried": [
  "A SECOND GOLD PASSAGE. The most valuable next input, and the only thing that separates the method from the tuning.",
  "Video frames at segment midpoints (frames_at.py) for the sub-second residue. Its own docstring warns the cut lags speech by about 2s and not by a fixed amount, which is worst exactly here in a rapid exchange, so it may not reach turns 2, 8 and 11 either.",
  "A speaker-embedding model with a shorter minimum window. wespeaker-voxceleb-resnet34-LM has a 0.6s floor, and that floor IS the residual -- this is the direct attack on it.",
  "NVIDIA NeMo Sortformer for stage A. Word gaps already give 100% boundary recall on this passage, so there is little left for it to win here; its documented over-segmentation bias would matter more against the long-monologue collapse.",
  "Speechmatics operating_point=standard, the current config schema, and the EU1 regional endpoint -- the three cheap untested variables on its one-cluster diarization failure.",
  "MaLLaM / SEA-LION for text-cue naming. The gold data caps text-only sensing near 83% on this passage, which the acoustic method already reaches, so this is now a tie-breaker for the residual rather than a primary route."
 ],
